<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed 24 civilians in Nigerian villages and bandits in Niger State murdered an immigration officer and burned his body, while fresh bandit attacks hit Borgu LGA. A Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. The United States blacklisted Nigeria for recruiting child soldiers and Mali added 2,400 recruits, including 800 women, to its reserve force. Ex-militants in Akwa Ibom pledged support for President Tinubu's re-election. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTFBxMnl6YzNOYW9nQTRBbWVabTNHakhTMnJDQ0VyWFNyVnpRbXg3SG9HTWtQNFA3dDRqNUhNU2ZoY0FDSUtWVnVWVFoxdl91eV94NmtlZTBjelpjdG5ObE9RUDgzclFSMVk?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Spectator Australia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxNSzcxdUhjQVpaalNqbHdVd1Vua0hHSDdaYkZoMFJGQVRiNFBQYlo1Ykdqdjc3TVRxUDBKMFEwYUF1RXhjd3NEdk9oQkJQMVRjUG1DbWtzc1JSWFN0bzVxTFBmZEo2aW1HX3pQN0VFUzNOUDhKZ1ZoZkg2ODkwd2tKRmdYY3BVSGVpWVFyZmZ2VVhfMUlubGhPbDV0U2NKakNWcS1QMS0xUWs2dW1sdXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;The News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxPbTk0WW45NXRjUjhaaXVFZTdkaWxMQzBnVHJxRzI0NG9SWTNWYTYyclhVd1h5cm5SRUNQM3BKc1RDODNjR2xsRHU5VDl5ZGVRQWZvQ1JsSEVYX0dRMWw4aTFXOHV0REp5ZXotdDNWeWp4OHNoZTlJeVBMdlFnTENfdXA4Z09CUzBvUTV2d2RhVEtLMnVFVDBjanhFYWRFVDA5Vm1rWVhiU3VMSHB2T2c?oc=5&quot;&gt;AIT LIVE&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUkFVX3lxTE9TQkoxR2UyWjVnY1N4XzBSbjJGbFhtYlBPVmwxU01lOTFTUVF0Z1ZhV1hIWlNjd2VHS2F0MWg5TmtoTHZrTTVpZTJxZE9QTk82RWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;